 "text": "Hey! How are you feeling? Stand seat on the frame and stand the bike up against something so it's horizontal. It should be level across the top tube. both feet should be on the pedals with the chain off the big front gear. Step foot of your shoe on the seat in the middle. It' fine. The seat post tells us where to position the seat bolt, and the seat bolt is what actually adjusts the seat. Does it look a bit like this? Then reverse one bolt. Turn the left one into the frame a few turns and seat will move up. You' need a short step stick made of wood or PVC. You can make one or anyone can buy one for you.",
